{"title":"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems\">2015 AMC 12A #16</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems\">2015 AMC 10A #21</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Francesca&#39;s_Irregular_Tetrahedron_Formula)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Francesca's Irregular Tetrahedron Formula)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Coord_Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Coord Bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ff29028b2432b4e2cf3d924ac82114813de066d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=5$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/6/f7661519159a6678741c369a2e897dfd24579670.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=3$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a5322c7f896502c208bbb4a354efc8d212620667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/d/bbd469ed9ff340d47afa0fd2b9a41b662a9fdfef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e867467073fae9550c977a21ee2cb19426c4f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=3$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25dc3032a86bd869e2b6f40a776ca03b979859eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=\\tfrac{12}5\\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"96\" height=\"23\" />.  What is the volume of the tetrahedron?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/2/a524c6c44a33bb8d04325509bee01c031d78186d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }3\\sqrt2\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }2\\sqrt5\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }\\dfrac{24}5\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }3\\sqrt3\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }\\dfrac{24}5\\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"478\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Drop altitudes of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> down from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Both will hit the same point; let this point be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Because both triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> are 3-4-5 triangles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/7/3873078e03dce6550ab5c8afd497da1f22b716af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CT = DT = \\dfrac{3\\cdot4}{5} = \\dfrac{12}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"184\" height=\"37\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef8c07853f9d3cafb46bc949a5f50b427a634496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CT^{2} + DT^{2} = 2\\left(\\frac{12}{5}\\right)^{2} = \\left(\\frac{12}{5}\\sqrt{2}\\right)^{2} = CD^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"350\" height=\"46\" />, it follows that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/252b4379bd7d4f56ca4cee487817e25303f43506.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CTD$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> is a right triangle, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/f/86fdb1aae2659b4341f6323860c7be113020d29f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CTD = 90^\\circ$\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />, and it follows that planes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> are perpendicular to each other. Now, we can treat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> as the base of the tetrahedron and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/4/264f0c33a54d96dace10debd80b92b6c2d80ddac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TD$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> as the height. Thus, the desired volume is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71b83ffd78ebc4a9e1f2052e7fb367c8019bd071.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[V = \\dfrac{1}{3} bh = \\dfrac{1}{3}\\cdot[ABC]\\cdot TD = \\dfrac{1}{3} \\cdot 6 \\cdot \\dfrac{12}{5} = \\dfrac{24}{5}\\]\" width=\"354\" height=\"37\" /> which is answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/5/515a189da60e45d14676657c952371171e2858e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } \\dfrac{24}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"69\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/6/b06e219dd296fa7c67e8a510d8b9dc842d9f822d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = \\dfrac{6}{5} \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"90\" height=\"37\" />, and so by the Pythagorean Theorem <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/0/70016046222cee7d5e67e05bea5a7621b9fb8bc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{153}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"97\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a216050437be6388710bc1358890e2cbcdcfc139.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{328}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"43\" />. Because the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> of tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> passes touches plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7ada763e99852a6e44a15d46cce3c3709a944d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, it is also an altitude of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. The area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> is, by Heron's Formula, given by\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecd7a18d42aa428cb4acd4a869efb7f0c32c7226.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16A^2 = 2a^2 b^2 + 2b^2 c^2 + 2c^2 a^2 - a^4 - b^4 - c^4 = -(a^2 + b^2 - c^2)^2 + 4a^2 b^2.\\]\" width=\"497\" height=\"19\" />\nSubstituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/a/f0afda05a52c5b7653505b24c3b3e35d10f27c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = AE, b = BE, c = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"180\" height=\"16\" /> and performing huge (but manageable) computations yield <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef72b5680321165fa9c6ad6b8f8afe99a9092ebd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A^2 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/a/3cad82faa3c807ce8a5d17e45573b0cf0562544a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 3\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the length of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> of the tetrahedron, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a994fa6023c98ea4fb6d75ddfa2c581f8f1c5583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE \\cdot h = 2A = 6\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"159\" height=\"21\" />. Our answer is thus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/417426f51d86f6b908bb87306831529d93a55064.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[V = \\dfrac{1}{3} Bh = \\dfrac{1}{3} h \\cdot BE \\cdot \\dfrac{6\\sqrt{2}}{5} = \\dfrac{24}{5},\\]\" width=\"267\" height=\"41\" />\nand so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/5/515a189da60e45d14676657c952371171e2858e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } \\dfrac{24}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"69\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to solution 1, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e6a9c34f55e6bf9647cc400a91a99004d5ca42a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CTD$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is an isosceles right triangle. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is perpendicular to the plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/252b4379bd7d4f56ca4cee487817e25303f43506.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CTD$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. So, we can cut tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> into 2 tetrahedrons <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5c9020d08ccdd4c1451fa07d8331ff43a56abde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACTD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50ec58caf6150c829b01f41d132b75d6b98e2b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCTD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e6a9c34f55e6bf9647cc400a91a99004d5ca42a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CTD$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> as their common base, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69c58bfed7dc75f115a1dd50937a19ab6529aefa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BT$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d5b93dbd5e47d3865c56f03ec1213bb82256a67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AT$\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> as their heights.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/e/00eb2e5da3586a39b7c2459b636f28806e91753e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[CTD]=\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot CT \\cdot DT=\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{12}{5} \\cdot \\frac{12}{5}= \\frac{72}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"329\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/8/0b82e26dac4af525adac3f418b6e40dcc50a09fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_{ABCD}=V_{ACDT}+V_{BCDT}=\\frac{1}{3} \\left([CTD] \\cdot AT + [CTD] \\cdot BT \\right)=\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot [CTD] \\cdot (AT+BT)=\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot [CTD] \\cdot AB  =\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{72}{25} \\cdot 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"919\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/c/3ec1089253412f95b92f45c34280a982b4a2d928.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } \\dfrac{24}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"89\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Francesca.27s_Irregular_Tetrahedron_Formula.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Francesca's_Irregular_Tetrahedron_Formula)\">Solution 4 (Francesca's Irregular Tetrahedron Formula)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Francesca&#39;s Irregular Tetrahedron Formula)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note: Please don't ever try doing this in an actual competition. It's fun to do, however.\n</p><p>Using Piero della Francesca's Theorem:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/1/b51a8896b736b897355aa3bf54e70a9102c47c6a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[V = \\frac{1}{12} \\left( \\sqrt{-a^2b^2c^2 - a^2d^2e^2 - b^2d^2f^2 - c^2e^2f^2 + a^2c^2d^2 + b^2c^2d^2 + a^2b^2e^2 + b^2c^2e^2 + b^2d^2e^2 + c^2d^2e^2 + a^2b^2f^2 + a^2c^2f^2 + a^2d^2f^2 + c^2d^2f^2 + a^2e^2f^2 + b^2e^2f^2 - c^4d^2 - c^2d^4 - b^4e^2 - b^2e^4 - a^4f^2 - a^2f^4} \\right)\\]\" width=\"1567\" height=\"37\" />\nSubstituting this all in... You get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/5/515a189da60e45d14676657c952371171e2858e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } \\dfrac{24}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"69\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~Banspeedrun\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Coord_Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Coord_Bash)\">Solution 5 (Coord Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Coord Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9f36b13a11a14accae8e072c0cf34d69267bb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/e/bbe2d2cf7bfa134edc87b4ff1d226f36512fa793.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/0/d309b4679ce5bb88697f5ec843bb45305aff225e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,3,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />. If we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />'s coordinates then the z-coordinate(the last coord) is the height we need since the rest of the coordinates have a z-coord of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Notice that we are given every distance from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, we can use basically satellite-type triangulation. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is at every point a radius from points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f642cbbd390b4882363ab6b5c2906dbf6be6cc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, or a sphere with the center at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f642cbbd390b4882363ab6b5c2906dbf6be6cc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. We can set up a system of equations to find where all 3 spheres intersect. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a50878a41ca5f7d0291167a975dd3dc88180e11.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split} (x-4)^2+(y-3)^2+z^2 &amp;=3^2 \\\\ x^2+y^2+z^2 &amp;=4^2 \\\\ (x-4)^2+y^2+z^2 &amp;=(\\tfrac{12}{5}\\sqrt2)^2 \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"271\" height=\"79\" />\nSolving this system of equations gives you:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/d/59dad1d0d0a3d713eccfa2f2aa6f631aca26be46.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split} x &amp;=\\frac{64}{25} \\\\ y &amp;=\\frac{48}{25} \\\\ z &amp;=\\frac{12}{5}  \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"54\" height=\"123\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the value we need, we can now solve for the volume. The base is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e8552bb741457e029577335aaba59343af93f09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3*4}{2}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/9/83995a2c0292c53201ae28e296a8ebcbc0f9097b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split} V &amp;=\\frac{1}{3}bh \\\\ V &amp;=\\frac{1}{3}(6)(\\frac{12}{5}) \\\\ V &amp;=\\frac{72}{15} \\\\ V &amp;=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\dfrac{24}{5}} \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"109\" height=\"177\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1J_P0tXszLQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1J_P0tXszLQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ckRtrNuNgk4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ckRtrNuNgk4</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A\">2015 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.